    "\n",
    "## 8: Encoding Categorical Variables\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why encode?\n",
    "ML models understand numbers, not text. We must convert every categorical column to a numeric representation.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Two main approaches:**\n",
    "\n",
    "| Method | How it works | Best for |\n",
    "|--------|-------------|----------|\n",
    "| **Label Encoding** | Assigns an integer to each category (Male=0, Female=1) | Binary or ordinal categories |\n",
    "| **One-Hot Encoding** | Creates a new 0/1 column for each category | Nominal (no order) categories with few unique values |\n",
    "\n",
    "For this dataset we will use **Label Encoding** for all categorical columns. It is simpler, works well with tree-based models (Random Forest, XGBoost), and keeps the number of columns manageable."
   ]
  },
