    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 9: Feature Scaling\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why scale features?\n",
    "Some models (e.g. Logistic Regression) are sensitive to the **magnitude** of features. If `tenure` ranges 0–72 but `TotalCharges` ranges 0–9000, the model might give unfair weight to TotalCharges simply because its numbers are bigger.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Method | Formula | When to use |\n",
    "|--------|---------|-------------|\n",
    "| **Standardisation (Z-score)** | (x − mean) / std | Most general-purpose; centres data around 0 |\n",
    "| **Min-Max Normalisation** | (x − min) / (max − min) | When you need values strictly in [0, 1] |\n",
    "\n",
    "Tree-based models (Random Forest, XGBoost) are **not** affected by scale, but Logistic Regression **is**. We will scale features for all models to keep things consistent."
   ]
  },
