    "---\n",
    "## 10: Train / Validation Split\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why split the data?\n",
    "If we train and evaluate on the **same** data, the model can just memorise answers this is called **overfitting**. It will look great on training data but fail on new customers.\n",
    "\n",
    "By holding out a portion as a **validation set**, we simulate Kaggle's hidden test and get an honest estimate of our model's performance.\n",
    "\n",
    "We use an 80/20 split and **stratify** by the target to ensure both halves have the same churn ratio."
   ]
