    "\n",
    "## Model 1. Logistic Regression\n",
    "\n",
    "### What It Does\n",
    "\n",
    "Imagine plotting every customer on a graph. Blue dots = stayed, Red dots = churned.\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Monthly Charges\n",
    "     |        🔴 🔴 🔴\n",
    "     |     🔴 🔴 🔴\n",
    "     |___________← draws this straight line\n",
    "     |  🔵 🔵 \n",
    "     | 🔵 🔵 🔵\n",
    "     |_________________ Tenure\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Logistic Regression simply **draws one straight line** to separate churners from non-churners. Everyone on the left side = probably stays. Everyone on the right side = probably churns.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Real Life Analogy\n",
    "Think of a bank deciding who gets a loan. They say:\n",
    "> *\"If income is above $50,000 AND age is above 25 → approve. Otherwise → reject.\"*\n",
    "\n",
    "That is a straight line decision. Simple, fast, explainable.\n",
    "\n",
    "### For Churn It Learns Things Like\n",
    "> *\"If tenure is low AND monthly charges are high → likely to churn\"*\n",
    "\n",
    "### Strengths and Weaknesses\n",
    "\n",
    "| Strengths | Weaknesses |\n",
    "|-----------|-----------|\n",
    "| Very fast to train | Cannot learn curved/complex patterns |\n",
    "| Easy to explain to business | Needs feature scaling |\n",
    "| Great starting baseline | Struggles with many interacting features |\n"
   ]
