    "## Model 3. Gradient Boosting\n",
    "\n",
    "### What It Does\n",
    "\n",
    "This is where it gets clever. Instead of 300 independent trees voting, Gradient Boosting builds trees **one by one** - and each new tree specifically focuses on fixing what the previous tree got wrong.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Step By Step\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Step 1: Tree 1 makes predictions\n",
    "        Got Sneha right ✅  Got Sanskar wrong ❌  Got Sakshi right ✅\n",
    "\n",
    "Step 2: Tree 2 looks at mistakes\n",
    "        \"Sanskar was wrong - let me focus extra hard on customers like Sanskar\"\n",
    "        Got Sanskar right ✅  Got someone else wrong ❌\n",
    "\n",
    "Step 3: Tree 3 looks at NEW mistakes\n",
    "        \"Let me fix the new mistakes...\"\n",
    "\n",
    "...repeat 300 times...\n",
    "\n",
    "Final: All 300 trees combined = very accurate model\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Real Life Analogy\n",
    "\n",
    "Think of a student taking practice exams:\n",
    "- **Exam 1** → scores 60%. Reviews wrong answers.\n",
    "- **Exam 2** → focuses on weak topics. Scores 72%. Reviews wrong answers again.\n",
    "- **Exam 3** → focuses on remaining weak spots. Scores 81%.\n",
    "- After 300 practice exams → becomes an expert.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each attempt specifically targets previous failures. That is **Gradient Boosting**.\n",
    "\n",
    "### For Churn It Learns Things Like\n",
    "> *\"First tree gets easy churners right - obvious cases like 1 month tenure, $90 bill\"*\n",
    "> *\"Second tree focuses on tricky cases - maybe senior citizens with long tenure but high bills\"*\n",
    "> *\"By tree 300 it is catching very subtle patterns\"*\n",
    "\n",
    "### Strengths and Weaknesses\n",
    "\n",
    "| Strengths | Weaknesses |\n",
    "|-----------|-----------|\n",
    "| Very high accuracy | Slow to train |\n",
    "| Catches subtle patterns | Can overfit if not careful |\n",
    "| Great for imbalanced data | Many settings to tune |\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n"
   ]
  },
