    "## Model 4. XGBoost\n",
    "\n",
    "### What It Does\n",
    "\n",
    "XGBoost is basically Gradient Boosting with several smart improvements added on top. The X stands for **eXtreme** - it is an extreme version of Gradient Boosting.\n",
    "\n",
    "### What Makes It Different\n",
    "\n",
    "| Feature | Regular Gradient Boosting | XGBoost |\n",
    "|---------|--------------------------|---------|\n",
    "| Speed | Slow | **10x faster** |\n",
    "| Overfitting protection | Basic | **Built-in regularisation** |\n",
    "| Missing values | You must handle them | **Handles automatically** |\n",
    "| Parallel processing | No | **Uses all CPU cores** |\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Regularisation Part Simply Explained\n",
    "\n",
    "Regular Gradient Boosting is like a student who **memorises** every single practice exam answer including weird edge cases. XGBoost adds a penalty:\n",
    "\n",
    "> *\"Do not make my trees too complicated. Keep them simple and general.\"*\n",
    "\n",
    "This means XGBoost generalises better to new unseen customers - exactly what you need for Kaggle test data.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why XGBoost Wins on Kaggle\n",
    "\n",
    "Between 2015 and 2023, XGBoost won **more Kaggle competitions than any other single algorithm.** For churn prediction specifically it works brilliantly because:\n",
